.TH KEYLATCH\-PROXY 1 "2026-10-16" "keylatch" "Keylatch Manual"
.SH NAME
keylatch\-proxy \- manage the local CONNECT proxy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B keylatch proxy
.RB { up | down | status }
.RI [ flags ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
\fBkeylatch proxy\fR manages a local HTTP CONNECT interception proxy that
injects credentials into outbound provider calls. The gateway and the proxy
start and stop independently. The proxy is experimental.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B up
Start the proxy. \fB\-\-port\fR sets the listener port (default 8888);
\fB\-\-detach\fR runs it in the background.
.TP
.B down
Stop the proxy.
.TP
.B status
Print whether the proxy is running.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR keylatch (1),
.BR keylatch\-run (1)
